    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6b287489aa40c73cc68a90d40cec6987fc8dc358be33d24521cac5fc470ca070",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source turns local pole behavior into a global quadratic height in two stages: valuation lemmas translate the elliptic group law into placewise identities, and the residue-degree-weighted product formula cancels the remaining coordinate-difference terms to prove the parallelogram law for d. Since d is visibly nonnegative on integer combinations, Lemma 3 then forces every associated binary height form to have nonpositive discriminant.",
